From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: brennoflavio <contato@brennoflavio.com.br>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 10:29:15 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] webapi: synthesize canvas output from lightweight draw
 records
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Record clipped solid rectangles, clears, synthetic text glyphs and visible
putImageData snapshots instead of allocating a persistent canvas bitmap.
Share native paint/readback behavior between regular and offscreen 2D
contexts. Reuse the existing Mac font advance model for text placement;
small deterministic 5x7 masks do not claim CoreText rasterization fidelity.

Generate dimension-correct RGBA PNGs on demand with the standard-library
fastest DEFLATE encoder, CRCs, and a 4 KiB output tile. Pixel reads replay
only intersecting spans and agree with the generated image. No graphics,
font, image codec or GPU dependency is added. Retained memory follows draw
records and explicit visible pixel uploads, not canvas width times height.
Discard fully covered records on opaque replacements, clears and uploads,
recycling obsolete pixel snapshots and retaining command capacity for reuse.

Keep source-over alpha, supported style save/restore, text alignment and
baseline, maxWidth, dirty pixel uploads, and negative readback dimensions
coherent within this bounded model. Resize—including same-value attribute
assignments—resets supported state and content. Match internal dimensions
to reflected HTML integer parsing. Preserve explicit-null numeric coercion.
Snapshot Blob bytes at invocation while retaining asynchronous delivery and
cancellation cleanup. Keep the existing zero-size and PNG fallback behavior.

Leave paths, transforms, gradients, shadows, image decoding, JPEG/WebP
encoding and exact Mac typography outside the patch. Non-overwritten draw
history can still grow; this is a display-list mock, not a general renderer.

Update existing canvas assertions tied to the fixed 1x1 PNG and negative
readback rejection; add no tests or benchmark predicate changes. Temporary
validation covers 93 checks including decoded PNG CRCs/dimensions/pixels,
Blob equality and snapshots, native shape, regular/offscreen/worker/iframe
and isolated-world parity, resets, integer/coercion regressions, navigation,
and partial-update memory reuse. Upstream tests pass (1658/1658).
